    ],
    "_comment": "Algorithm-level family mirroring rmsnorm2d: one folder per algorithm, every kernel carries its own dtype+N constraints. LayerNorm subtracts the row mean and adds a per-column Beta (bias) on top of the scale by Gamma; the ABI is (X,Gamma,Beta,Y,M,N,eps). Static-N kernels bake N (exact N== match, tuned per shape); runtime-N '_dyn_' kernels read N from the i32 arg and match any N that is a multiple of vec, giving a general catch-all (parity with rmsnorm2d_dynamic). Catalog::candidatesFor gathers by op_kind and gates per-kernel on dtype+N, so f16/bf16, every static N tier, and the dynamic catch-all coexist with no engine change.",
